# .dockerignore for the commit-image build (`docker build -f mayhem/Dockerfile .`).
#
# BuildKit gives `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` full PRECEDENCE over the context-root
# .dockerignore, so this file — not sui's own — is what applies to our build. That matters
# here: sui ships a root .dockerignore tuned for its *deployment* images which drops `*.md`
# and `docker/`, and (more importantly) does NOT drop `external-crates/move/target/`, the
# ~900 MB cargo build directory a local dev/gate run leaves behind. Shipping it would bloat
# the context and the image for no benefit — mayhem/build.sh rebuilds everything in-image.
#
# Goal: bake in the FULL repo INCLUDING .git history (SPEC §6.2 item 2 — the grader and the
# PATCH tier read it), dropping only build outputs and local cruft. This is a dev image, not
# a minimal one. In particular we deliberately KEEP every upstream Rust source and test
# fixture, since mayhem/test.sh runs the project's own bytecode-verifier / binary-format
# suites out of the image (see docs/netnew-worker-prompt.md §4b on oracle collapse).

# ── cargo build outputs (regenerated by mayhem/build.sh) ─────────────────────
/target/
**/target/

# ── JS/TS workspace outputs (sui is a polyglot monorepo) ─────────────────────
**/node_modules/
**/.turbo/
**/.next/

# ── infra / local cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.terraform/
**/__pycache__/

# ── editor / OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
